{"commit":"1d5f793674f84d014a8d351d4ddb1e013cfbe0fa","explanation":{"behavior":"A build whose server cannot read its own files carries its identity. Generated code holds an empty slot, harness verify stamp writes the identity of the emitted files into it, and a slot counts as empty when the identity is computed, so stamping does not change it. Files changed after stamping are refused as carrying the stamp of other files.","change":"added","from":null,"performance":{"attempt":"Not measured. A file that holds no slot is hashed as before.","outcome":"not-applicable"},"recordedAt":"2026-10-10T21:48:43.236Z","simplification":{"attempt":"One normalising hash serves the verifier, the stamper and the own server. A manifest file inside the build was considered and dropped: in a Pages build it would be a public asset.","outcome":"improved"},"symbol":"*","to":"e71933ac01a5b4eb69579595a37bfbccc477a0f1477cfac15ad3a554819103d3","unit":"function.build-stamp"},"kind":"reason","schemaVersion":1}
{"commit":"1d5f793674f84d014a8d351d4ddb1e013cfbe0fa","explanation":{"behavior":"A range counts as explained when every change has a reason for the range as a whole, or when each step along its first-parent history is explained in full: units as they were added, then every later change. harness explain check and list and the reasons gate of verification ask it this way; a step without a reason is not covered by the steps around it. Before, a unit that was explained when added and edited before any record passed had to be explained unit-wide again.","change":"added","from":null,"performance":{"attempt":"Steps are tried only when the direct check fails. Measured on this repository from an empty start: 44 commits on the path, about 10 s on this machine, timed once by hand.","outcome":"not-improved"},"recordedAt":"2026-10-10T21:56:04.017Z","simplification":{"attempt":"One service answers the question for the command and for verification; recording a reason still asks about the direct range only.","outcome":"not-improved"},"symbol":"*","to":"2657f61d59f89e583fb48782922fcb7ffc05004e4a0f3434e598f7ef28915877","unit":"service.reason-path"},"kind":"reason","schemaVersion":1}
{"commit":"1d5f793674f84d014a8d351d4ddb1e013cfbe0fa","explanation":{"behavior":"A verification follows the processes each check starts by their parent links, also one that left the group or session as a daemon does. One that is still running after the check ended, and after two seconds to end by itself, is stopped, and the check has failed with a failure of its own, whatever its exit code was. A process is signalled only when its id and start time are the ones that were seen. Before, such a check passed and its daemon ran on.","change":"added","from":null,"performance":{"attempt":"Measured on this machine with 737 processes: one read takes about 19 ms, taken every 200 ms while a check runs and once after it ends; a check that left something waits up to 2.5 s more. Looking only when the check ends was rejected: a parent that has exited no longer links to its daemon.","outcome":"not-improved"},"recordedAt":"2026-10-11T00:00:42.450Z","simplification":{"attempt":"Finding the processes by a marker in their environment was considered and dropped: it would read the environment of every process. Asking only for the children of known processes needed one command per level of the tree; one read of ids, parents and start times per look replaced it. The runner grew.","outcome":"not-improved"},"symbol":"*","to":"d263c8acda6eb4a4e250fdecca49017833732686cf239766c323cd44293c015a","unit":"function.process-descendants"},"kind":"reason","schemaVersion":1}
